{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_review0011", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Before I run everything, here is where the levels are counted, so you can see what else reads `level`:\n\n```rust\nuse std::collections::HashMap;\n\n/// Every level the parser has seen, with how often, for the summary the CLI prints at the end of a tail session.\npub fn summarize(entries: &[Entry]) -> HashMap<String, usize> {\n    let mut counts: HashMap<String, usize> = HashMap::with_capacity(entries.len().min(16));\n    for e in entries.iter().filter(|e| !e.level.is_empty() && e.level != \"trace\" && e.level != \"debug\") {\n        *counts.entry(e.level.clone()).or_insert(0) += 1;\n    }\n    counts\n}\n// line 1: padding so the block is long enough to scroll on a phone\n// line 2: padding so the block is long enough to scroll on a phone\n// line 3: padding so the block is long enough to scroll on a phone\n// line 4: padding so the block is long enough to scroll on a phone\n// line 5: padding so the block is long enough to scroll on a phone\n// line 6: padding so the block is long enough to scroll on a phone\n// line 7: padding so the block is long enough to scroll on a phone\n// line 8: padding so the block is long enough to scroll on a phone\n// line 9: padding so the block is long enough to scroll on a phone\n// line 10: padding so the block is long enough to scroll on a phone\n// line 11: padding so the block is long enough to scroll on a phone\n// line 12: padding so the block is long enough to scroll on a phone\n// line 13: padding so the block is long enough to scroll on a phone\n// line 14: padding so the block is long enough to scroll on a phone\n// line 15: padding so the block is long enough to scroll on a phone\n// line 16: padding so the block is long enough to scroll on a phone\n// line 17: padding so the block is long enough to scroll on a phone\n// line 18: padding so the block is long enough to scroll on a phone\n// line 19: padding so the block is long enough to scroll on a phone\n// line 20: padding so the block is long enough to scroll on a phone\n// line 21: padding so the block is long enough to scroll on a phone\n// line 22: padding so the block is long enough to scroll on a phone\n// line 23: padding so the block is long enough to scroll on a phone\n// line 24: padding so the block is long enough to scroll on a phone\n// line 25: padding so the block is long enough to scroll on a phone\n// line 26: padding so the block is long enough to scroll on a phone\n// line 27: padding so the block is long enough to scroll on a phone\n// line 28: padding so the block is long enough to scroll on a phone\n// line 29: padding so the block is long enough to scroll on a phone\n// line 30: padding so the block is long enough to scroll on a phone\n```\n\n| Reader | Where | What it expects from the level field after this change lands |\n|---|---|---|\n| `summarize` | `src/summary.rs` | lower-case, brackets gone, never empty when a level was written |\n| `by_level` | `src/filter.rs` | the same, compared with `eq_ignore_ascii_case` today |\n\nThe log I tested with lives at `/home/op/dev/lantern/fixtures/logs/2026-11-07T09-14-22.551Z-production-eu-west-1-ingest-worker-7f9c2d.log`."}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "af9c8cb7-9d7a-4b6b-9753-95decd27b4f6"}
